data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"# QA Verification Report — Dispatch d002\\n\\n**Repository:** hello-app  \\n**Commit under test:** `0cf727b` (`refs/campaign/orchestrator`)  \\n**Date:** 2026-09-21  \\n**Tester:** qa agent\\n\\n## Commands run\\n\\n```sh\\ngit checkout refs/campaign/orchestrator\\nnpm install\\nnpm run build\\nnpm run dev\\n```\\n\\nBuild completed successfully (`vite build`, 1761 modules transformed, dist generated).  \\nDev server started on `0.0.0.0:5173` as documented.\\n\\nRendered output was inspected with a headless Chromium browser via a Puppeteer script (`/tmp/verify.js`). Viewport was set to 1280×800.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n### Design-system components\\nAll required `data-component` attributes are present in the rendered page:\\n- `Header` — present\\n- `Footer` — present\\n- `Button` — present\\n- `Card` — present\\n- `Page` — present\\n- `AppShell` — present\\n\\n### Header and Footer\\n- Header title is exactly **\\\"Hello App\\\"**.\\n- Footer text is exactly **\\\"Built with @codesweep-ai/ui\\\"** and centered.\\n\\n### Greeting\\n- Text is exactly **\\\"Hello, world!\\\"**.\\n- Rendered as a large, bold, centered heading.\\n- Computed styles: `font-size: 32px`, `font-weight: 700`, `text-align: center`.\\n- Initial resolved colour: `rgb(96, 165, 250)` (from `var(--color-info)`).\\n- The colour is applied via an inline style using CSS variables (`var(--color-info)`, etc.), not hard-coded hex values.\\n\\n### Buttons and colour changes\\nButtons appear in order with labels **Blue, Green, Amber, Red**.\\n\\n| Button | Active colour resolved value | Active button variant |\\n|--------|------------------------------|-----------------------|\\n| Blue   | `rgb(96, 165, 250)`          | primary               |\\n| Green  | `rgb(52, 211, 153)`          | primary               |\\n| Amber  | `rgb(245, 158, 11)`          | primary               |\\n| Red    | `rgb(248, 113, 113)`        | primary               |\\n\\nFor each click, exactly one button (the one whose label matches the greeting colour) has a non-transparent background (primary), while the other three have transparent backgrounds (secondary). All four clicks produce distinct greeting colours.\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n`package.json` lists `@codesweep-ai/ui`, `react`, and `react-dom`. It does **not** list the optional peers `mermaid`, `puppeteer`, `pixelmatch`, or `pngjs`.\\n\\n### Layout\\n- The **Card is visually centered both vertically and horizontally between the Header and Footer**.\\n- The greeting and button row are centered inside the Card.\\n- **Deviation:** the `Page` component itself does **not** fill the available viewport height between the Header and the Footer. Its rendered height is ~169 px, while the available content height is ~704 px (viewport 800 px − header 54 px − footer 42 px). The vertical centering is achieved by an additional wrapper `\u003cdiv\u003e` with inline custom CSS (`flex: 1 1 auto; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center`) placed around the `Page`. This wrapper, rather than `Page`, is what fills the height.\\n- Horizontal centering: the Card is offset from the exact horizontal center of the `Page` content area by ~4 px at 1280×800. This is within sub-pixel/rendering tolerance and visually centered.\\n\\n### Conclusion\\nThe application satisfies the functional requirements of the design: correct greeting, correct button labels, correct colour tokens, correct active-button variant behaviour, correct design-system components, correct dependencies, and the Card is visually centered between Header and Footer.\\n\\nThe one notable deviation from `DESIGN.md` is the layout implementation: the `Page` component is wrapped in a custom flex `\u003cdiv\u003e` to obtain full-height vertical centering, instead of `Page` itself filling the available viewport height. The visual outcome is correct, but it introduces custom inline layout CSS rather than relying solely on the design-system utilities.\\n\\n## No code changes\\nThe application code was not modified; this report reflects verification only.\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-report.md\"}","name":"write"},"id":"write_49","index":0,"type":"function"}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789959904,"id":"chatcmpl-632f572ba3d94901a40b97a3c6578ee3","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

